# Away and around in Russian: отнести, обойти, сойти
subtitle: "Russian от-, об- and с- on verbs of motion: carry a box away, walk round the house, go up and down the stairs."
tags: ["russian","verbs of motion","russian prefixes","отнести","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/motion-prefixes","grammar/verbs-of-motion"]
thumb: "band \"Three little fronts, three ways to move\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Coming and going in Russian: ухожу, приезжаю, сходи","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/134-russian-come-and-go.cast"}

