audio:
  lang: en
  lines:
    '|a||Away and around in Russian: отнести, обойти, сойти':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6640
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Russian от-, об- and с- on verbs of motion: carry a box away, walk round the house, go up and down the stairs.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:14gsy7t'
    '|a||Away, round, down off: what do от-, об- and с- add to a verb of motion? Сентя́брь, суббо́та: Masha''s boxes have come from Moscow.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13600
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Её кварти́ра на тре́тьем этаже́, и я помога́ю. Послу́шайте.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:rg32hk'
    '|b||Том, отнеси́ э́ту коро́бку наве́рх, пожа́луйста.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3000
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:nbm5vk'
    '|a||Опя́ть по ле́стнице?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2080
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|b||Да, ли́фта нет. Поднима́йся по ле́стнице.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3040
      voice: gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated
    '|a||Хорошо́. Отойди́ от две́ри — коро́бка тяжёлая!':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3760
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Where should the box go?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1680
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Наве́рх: up, to the flat.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2440
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Why does Tom take the stairs?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2320
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Ли́фта нет: there''s no lift.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2720
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||What does Tom ask Masha to do? (от две́ри = from the door)':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5800
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Отойди́ от две́ри: step away from the door.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4000
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Посмотри́те. Отнеси́ э́ту коро́бку наве́рх.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3560
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Коро́бка: a box. On нести́, to carry, от- adds away: carry it off, and leave it there.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:azcraj'
    '|a||Отнести́ is on foot. By taxi it''s везти́, with the same от-: отвезти́.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:127pv02'
    '|a||Кни́ги Ма́ша отвезёт на рабо́ту.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:17gr4dk'
    '|a||Отойди́ от две́ри! You know подойти́ к две́ри from lesson 107: up to the door.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1tw7t9m'
    '|a||Отойти́ от две́ри: away from it. От- on the verb, and от after it: away, twice. Then the of-form: от две́ри, от окна́.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:j9344r'
    '|a||Такси́ у до́ма. А вход? Вход с друго́й стороны́: on the other side. Сторона́ is a side.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1s8wgj7'
    '|a||На́до обойти́ дом вокру́г: walk round it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1rl8hd7'
    '|a||Вокру́г means around. Об- on the verb mostly says the same, round something, so вокру́г can go: обойти́ дом.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:15unlzb'
    '|a||А такси́ мо́жет объе́хать дом: drive round it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:17j0mhz'
    '|a||Ли́фта нет. Есть ле́стница: the stairs.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:9l7780'
    '|a||Up the stairs is подня́ться, and наве́рх is up. Я подниму́сь на тре́тий эта́ж.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1073snm'
    '|a||Down is спусти́ться вниз: вниз, down. No prefix rule here: learn the two as a pair.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1ahnjaf'
    '|a||From lesson 107 you know five fronts, each with its little word.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:7xl7qx'
    '|a||Тепе́рь три но́вых. От- with от: away from. Отойти́ от две́ри.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:i2wz9b'
    '|a||Об- with вокру́г, or with nothing: round. Обойти́ дом вокру́г.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:c7ivgd'
    '|a||And с- with с: down off something. Сойти́ с авто́буса: to get off the bus.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1t8ebsa'
    '|a||Посмотри́те: the front and the little word usually say the same thing.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:atf190'
    '|a||Запо́лните про́пуски. The little word after the verb gives you its front.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:nfktn4'
    '|a||Запо́лните про́пуски.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:s3paii'
    '|a||Ма́ша отошла́ от окна́.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2320
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Том обошёл дом вокру́г.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:10ra4sc'
    '|a||Я сошёл с авто́буса.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1lcn695'
    '|a||Мы перешли́ че́рез мост. Молоде́ц!':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1rsib1a'
    '|a||Послу́шайте и напиши́те.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1a5u76h'
    '|a||Отойди́ от две́ри!':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1kcddd1'
    '|a||Напиши́те.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1320
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Пра́вильно! Отойди́ от две́ри.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2720
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Напиши́те по-ру́сски: walk round the house.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3520
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Напиши́те: Walk round the house.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:saiyli'
    '|a||Пра́вильно! Об-, round the house.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3400
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Ещё одна́ коро́бка. Tap Practise after the dialogue, and be Masha.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5120
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Шесть вопро́сов. У́тром: the taxi brings the first boxes. Послу́шайте.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:p39dve'
    '|a||Ма́ша, мы у до́ма, но я не ви́жу вход.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:pvxnor'
    '|b||Вы с друго́й стороны́ до́ма.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1840
      voice: gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated
    '|a||А как туда́ пройти́?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1800
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|b||Обойди́ дом вокру́г. Я жду на тре́тьем этаже́!':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2880
      voice: gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated
    '|a||Where has the taxi stopped?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2200
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||С друго́й стороны́ до́ма: on the other side of the house.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4480
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||How does Tom get to the entrance?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2920
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Обойди́ дом вокру́г: round the house.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4040
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Now the little words. Вы́берите.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3360
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Вы́берите: от, с or к?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1d0d95e'
    '|a||Том отошёл от окна́.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2200
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Ма́ша сошла́ с ле́стницы.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1fvpio1'
    '|a||Ма́ша подошла́ к две́ри.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:cyd6ca'
    '|a||Walk round the house! Вы́берите.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:100jhzf'
    '|a||Об- is round.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2560
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Отнеси́ коро́бку наве́рх, пожа́луйста.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2360
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Напиши́те: I''ll go up to the third floor.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4120
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Пра́вильно! Подня́ться: я подниму́сь.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3880
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||You got 6 of 6.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2080
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||So: от- goes or takes away, об- goes round, с- comes down off. And the stairs: подня́ться, спусти́ться.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:vqrnvy'
    '|b||Все коро́бки на тре́тьем этаже́. Спаси́бо, Том! Тепе́рь чай.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4720
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:grggnn'
    '|a||Next time: coming and going, every day.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1tj4f6g'
    '|a||Отнеси́ коро́бку наве́рх: up, to the flat.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3200
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Отойди́ от две́ри: step away from the door. The box is heavy.':
